-- WHY li-b2g-receive CARRIES mandate_scope = 'none' AND NOT 'b2g_only'.
--
-- Corrected 27 August 2026, after tests/map-tiles-agree.mjs refused the
-- country: "the map says B2G only -- government mandate real, no B2B
-- mandate, but the tiles say B2G VOLUNTARY / B2B NO_MANDATE". It was
-- right, and the milestone was the side that was wrong.
--
-- 'b2g_only' means a mandate restricted to invoicing the government --
-- a duty on the SUPPLIER to issue. Liechtenstein has no such duty. What
-- it has is a duty on the contracting AUTHORITY to receive and process,
-- which is the third value's territory exactly: real and binding, but
-- not itself an e-invoicing-mandate-scope fact.
--
-- Cyprus is the precedent and it runs the same way. Its 2020 milestone,
-- "Sub-central public bodies must also receive e-invoices", is on the
-- board with mandate_scope = 'none' -- and Cyprus's B2G tile reads
-- VOLUNTARY, as Liechtenstein's does. The two off-board Cypriot and
-- Czech receive milestones do carry 'b2g_only', which is survivable
-- because The Map only reads on-board rows; putting one on the board is
-- what surfaces the disagreement.
--
-- The lesson generalises past this country: mandate_scope answers "what
-- kind of obligation is this, and on whom", not "what is this milestone
-- about". A receive duty is about B2G and is not a B2G mandate.
